{
  "id": "R019Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "X-ray",
  "description": "An X-ray uses brief radiation exposure to create 2D images of bones and internal structures. This quick, painless outpatient test typically takes just minutes. Depending on what's being evaluated, images focus on specific body areas, bones, chest, abdomen, or spine. X-rays are the first-line imaging for fractures, infections, arthritis, and lung disease. Your doctor gets results quickly to guide diagnosis and treatment. You go home immediately with minimal radiation exposure, far less than other imaging tests. The cost of this procedure may vary depending on the complexity involved. Categories include lower extremity, head/neck/upper extremity, chest/pelvis/abdomen, bone length, spine, and gi contrast.",
